# Rust bins
target
target-windows
target-linux

# Packaging and build artifacts, kept local on purpose -- nothing under build/
# is published. That includes the Debian and Windows scripts, version.json, and
# the whole Flatpak tree.
#
# Flathub still works: the submitted manifests are self-contained. They carry
# the desktop file, metainfo, icon and D-Bus service file as their own sources,
# so nothing here has to exist in the tagged source tree -- Flathub builds the
# Rust code and LICENSE, nothing else. Reference copies of what was submitted
# live in build/linux/flatpak/{marco,polo}/*.flathub.yml on the working copy.
build/

# internal dev code
.dev
.claude
.VSCodeCounter

# Program specific
tests/settings/settings.ron